+## Original-resolution delivery — no resizing of client originals
 
-| Key | What it does |
-|---|---|
-| `formspreeId` | **Connect the forms to your email.** Create a free form at [formspree.io](https://formspree.io) (free tier = 50 submissions/month), copy the ID from your endpoint `https://formspree.io/f/XXXXXXXX` into this field. Until set, the booking + contract forms gracefully fall back to opening the visitor's email app pre-filled. |
-| `email` / `phoneDisplay` / `whatsapp` | Contact details shown around the site. |
-| `instagram` | Your handle **without** the `@`. The Instagram links appear automatically once set. |
-| `salt` | Secret string used to hash client gallery logins. **Change it once before going live** (any long random string), then update the same value in `tools/new_gallery.py`. |
+Both the managed uploader and the legacy export tool now preserve uploaded/source
+originals **byte-for-byte**. The old 2000px download cap is removed. JPEG, PNG, WebP,
+AVIF and TIFF formats are supported; originals retain their existing format and
+embedded metadata. Only **separate viewing copies** are resized and compressed.
 
----
+- Managed viewing copies: WebP, up to 480/960/1600px on the long edge, no upscaling.
+- Managed client originals: private files behind server authorization and expiry checks.
+- Managed multi-photo downloads: streamed ZIPs containing unchanged originals, without
+  requiring all files in the browser's memory.
+- Preview safety limits never silently downsize originals. An exceptionally large
+  client original can use a preview-unavailable placeholder instead.
+- Hosting byte limits, free disk space and network/streaming constraints still apply.
+  They must be configured for the intended deliveries; they are not resolution caps.
+- Original EXIF/GPS metadata is preserved. Remove sensitive metadata before uploading
+  if a particular delivery requires it.
 
