+## Privacy: managed versus legacy galleries
 
-Each tile's cover is picked at random from that gallery's photos on every page
-load, so no separate cover image needs maintaining.
+**Managed deliveries** enforce access on the server. Client codes are hashed;
+private originals, session records and upload data live outside publicly served
+paths. Expiry and unpublishing block further access. Replacing a code revokes existing
+client sessions. Copies already downloaded cannot be recalled.
 
-### Client portal — selection & downloads
+**Legacy static galleries**, including the demos and anything committed under
+`galleries/`, are public files. Hash-shaped folder names, browser-side expiry and
+`robots.txt` do not provide confidentiality. Public Git history remains public.
+Use the managed uploader or another protected service for real private deliveries.
 
-The gallery toolbar has **Select photos** (tap photos to pick, or Select all),
-**Download all**, and **Request prints**. Downloads are bundled into a single
-**.zip** (via JSZip from CDN, with a graceful one-by-one fallback if the CDN
-is blocked). A floating action bar tracks the selection.
+The legacy generator is still available for approved public exports:
 
----
